1
00:00:00,213 --> 00:00:04,013
[奢华超市] This is Erewhon, the most expensive grocery store in the world.

2
00:00:04,013 --> 00:00:06,135
But it is so much more than that.

3
00:00:06,135 --> 00:00:13,411
It's a status symbol, a cultural phenomenon, and a place where celebrities go and spend more on a smoothie than most people spend on dinner.

4
00:00:13,411 --> 00:00:27,778
While other luxury grocers like Whole Foods might charge you a premium, Erewhon somehow convinced an enclave of Los Angeles that purchases like a single $20 Japanese strawberry or $40 sea moss shell, whatever the f*** that is, are reasonable purchases.&nbsp;

5
00:00:27,778 --> 00:00:29,585
And people aren't just willing to pay.

6
00:00:29,585 --> 00:00:31,030
They are lining up to pay.

7
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:32,718
The question is, why?

8
00:00:32,718 --> 00:00:38,402
What's the business strategy that turned a tiny health store into LA's most exclusive food spot?

9
00:00:38,402 --> 00:00:45,605
Because as fun as it is to poke fun at some of this stuff, I figure there's got to be more to it than overpriced produce and celebrity spotting.

10
00:00:45,605 --> 00:00:46,466
So guess what?

11
00:00:46,466 --> 00:00:47,468
I dug into it.

12
00:00:47,468 --> 00:00:57,141
And today we're investigating how Erewhon created a business model that's part grocery store, part venture capital firm for wellness brands, and part social club for the wellness elite.

13
00:00:57,141 --> 00:01:01,677
Let's discuss.

14
00:01:01,677 --> 00:01:02,946
It's actually really good.

15
00:01:02,946 --> 00:01:09,437
Now, before we get into the business strategy, which is super interesting and a little surprising, I'm not here to yank your chain.

16
00:01:09,437 --> 00:01:11,909
[门店体验] So we're going to start with the Erewhon experience.

17
00:01:11,909 --> 00:01:18,042
You walk in and are greeted off to the side here with a smoothie bar, lots of prepared food, and a delicious hot food bar.

18
00:01:18,042 --> 00:01:21,220
The overall aesthetic feels very open and airy.

19
00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:27,534
We have light wood finishes, minimal but luxurious design elements like the light fixtures, premium food displays.

20
00:01:27,534 --> 00:01:29,184
Bottom line, it's clean.

21
00:01:29,184 --> 00:01:31,204
It's extremely orderly.

22
00:01:31,204 --> 00:01:33,435
Nothing is out of place.

23
00:01:33,435 --> 00:01:34,818
And it feels healthy.

24
00:01:34,818 --> 00:01:36,884
I feel like I'm in a health food store.

25
00:01:36,884 --> 00:01:38,147
Good job, Erewhon.

26
00:01:38,147 --> 00:01:43,013
But if you think you're going to fill up your entire fridge at a reasonable price, you're sorely mistaken.

27
00:01:43,013 --> 00:01:45,687
[天价商品] Let's look at some of the most unique products.

28
00:01:45,687 --> 00:01:47,946
Cut up dragon fruit for $25.

29
00:01:47,946 --> 00:01:51,296
Fancy balsamic saba dressing for $50.

30
00:01:51,296 --> 00:01:54,662
Some plant protein powder for $60.

31
00:01:54,662 --> 00:01:56,046
That's not that crazy.

32
00:01:56,046 --> 00:01:57,438
Mine's like $60.

33
00:01:57,438 --> 00:01:59,511
Ramanuka honey for $70.&nbsp;

34
00:01:59,511 --> 00:02:01,154
$32 Erewhon sauce.&nbsp;

35
00:02:01,154 --> 00:02:04,429
And you already saw the $20 Hailey Bieber smoothie out in Park Yamant.

36
00:02:04,429 --> 00:02:08,284
Alongside the other celebrity design smoothie options, all coming in at about $20.

37
00:02:08,284 --> 00:02:10,234
And then of course, the hot food bar.

38
00:02:10,234 --> 00:02:13,312
Profit margins on these puppies are nice and high, but more on that later.

39
00:02:13,312 --> 00:02:20,574
Some of the most popular items include the mac and cheese and the sushi sandwich.

40
00:02:20,574 --> 00:02:27,094
First reaction, first sip, $20 smoothie, which I would never buy except for a video.

41
00:02:27,094 --> 00:02:33,142
Cheers to you guys.

42
00:02:33,142 --> 00:02:35,907
Holy shit, it's really good.

43
00:02:35,907 --> 00:02:37,675
That's not even a fake reaction.

44
00:02:37,675 --> 00:02:38,234
Try it.

45
00:02:38,234 --> 00:02:39,686
That's one of the best things I've had.

46
00:02:39,686 --> 00:02:41,092
It's like coconutty and delicious.

47
00:02:41,092 --> 00:02:43,025
This is my filmer for the day, by the way.

48
00:02:43,025 --> 00:02:48,708
She also birthed me.

49
00:02:48,708 --> 00:02:52,161
It's more coconutty than I expected.

50
00:02:52,161 --> 00:02:58,331
[顾客体验] As for the customer experience, well, similar to Trader Joe's, these store footprints are pretty small.

51
00:02:58,331 --> 00:03:00,235
It gets pretty crowded in here.

52
00:03:00,235 --> 00:03:03,265
Remember, we're in LA, so most people are driving here.

53
00:03:03,265 --> 00:03:09,794
They're not pulling up on foot like I do in New York, which also means the parking lot gets pretty crowded with luxury cars.

54
00:03:09,794 --> 00:03:13,093
And the staff is super friendly and knowledgeable for product recommendations.

55
00:03:13,093 --> 00:03:25,368
Now to wrap this section up before diving into the interesting business model, I should mention that unlike the sea moss shell and adaptogenic mushrooms, there actually are a decent amount of items here that are normal and not exorbitantly expensive.

56
00:03:25,368 --> 00:03:43,018
You'll see brands that you recognize at other non-luxury grocery stores, like Faya Yogurt, Siggy's Yogurt, Kerrygold Butter I saw, Driscoll's Berries, and a lot of well-known protein bars, plus just some things that are kind of reasonably priced, like a lot of fun drinks, as long as they meet the Erewhon standard of ingredients, which we'll talk more about in a bit.

57
00:03:43,018 --> 00:03:49,024
However, most of the stuff here is more expensive when you compare it to competing grocers like Whole Foods.

58
00:03:49,024 --> 00:03:57,174
So what exactly are you paying for at Erewhon, and why are so many people willing to spend $300 or more on a single grocery run?

59
00:03:57,174 --> 00:04:00,674
Let's look into the founding principles of Erewhon and the business model today.

60
00:04:00,674 --> 00:04:07,073
[品牌起源] Beginning with Erewhon's origin, I knew that it had Japanese roots before writing the script, but I didn't know the specifics, so here's the rundown.

61
00:04:07,073 --> 00:04:14,573
It was founded in 1966 by husband and wife Michio and Aveline Kushi, who emigrated to the U.S. from Japan about 20 years earlier.

62
00:04:14,573 --> 00:04:26,639
The name Erewhon was derived from an 1872 satirical novel by Samuel Butler, which was about a utopia in which people were responsible for their own health and prosecuted for the crime of being ill.&nbsp;

63
00:04:26,639 --> 00:04:28,605
Obviously, this place doesn't exist.

64
00:04:28,605 --> 00:04:29,777
It's a nowhere place.

65
00:04:29,777 --> 00:04:33,480
And fun fact, Erewhon is an anagram of the word nowhere.

66
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:34,264
And this is interesting.

67
00:04:34,264 --> 00:04:50,651
The original Erewhon health food market was based on a Japanese macrobiotic diet, and this is all about balancing the supposed yin and yang elements of food and cookware, which in practice all comes down to reducing animal products, eating locally grown food that's in season, and consuming meals in moderation.

68
00:04:50,651 --> 00:05:03,202
Erewhon then expanded to Los Angeles in the 70s, filed for bankruptcy in 81, and the chain was then purchased by entrepreneur Tony Ntochi in 2011.&nbsp;

69
00:05:03,202 --> 00:05:11,187
Since Tony took over, Erewhon has expanded to one location to now 10 locations across LA, and Erewhon is looking to expand to different cities.

70
00:05:11,187 --> 00:05:12,097
More on that later.

71
00:05:12,097 --> 00:05:20,153
So that's the interesting origin and ownership change, but now let's take a look at the store's product strategy and the store economics.

72
00:05:20,153 --> 00:05:24,689
Fun fact, their product strategy was actually my favorite part to learn about when doing my research for this video.

73
00:05:24,689 --> 00:05:25,537
It's actually really cool.

74
00:05:25,537 --> 00:05:26,668
So let's discuss.

75
00:05:26,668 --> 00:05:35,445
[配料标准] You've probably deduced by now that Erewhon has a very strict standard for the items that it decides to sell, but you probably didn't guess that it was this strict.

76
00:05:35,445 --> 00:05:41,059
No refined sugars, no high fructose corn syrup, no artificial colors, flavors, or preservatives.

77
00:05:41,059 --> 00:05:42,189
All produce is organic.

78
00:05:42,189 --> 00:05:43,417
All dairy is grass-fed.

79
00:05:43,417 --> 00:05:45,476
All meat is grass-fed and free-range.

80
00:05:45,476 --> 00:05:46,799
Zero GMOs.

81
00:05:46,799 --> 00:05:47,592
You get the idea.

82
00:05:47,592 --> 00:05:51,975
And this has been dubbed the Erewhon standard, and they do not make compromises.

83
00:05:51,975 --> 00:05:52,748
I checked.

84
00:05:52,748 --> 00:05:54,552
But here's what I find the most fascinating.

85
00:05:54,552 --> 00:05:59,068
[品牌孵化] Erewhon has effectively become an incubator for up-and-coming health and wellness brands.&nbsp;

86
00:05:59,068 --> 00:06:07,183
When a brand approaches Erewhon, they face a vetting process that includes more than 100 different criteria, and every single ingredient is scrutinized.

87
00:06:07,183 --> 00:06:11,802
Products routinely get rejected for containing certain ingredients that most people wouldn't think twice about.

88
00:06:11,802 --> 00:06:14,298
Even certain natural flavors don't make the cut.

89
00:06:14,298 --> 00:06:20,617
Another really cool part, Erewhon often works directly with the brands to reformulate products specifically for their stores.

90
00:06:20,617 --> 00:06:27,181
So imagine being a small health food startup and hearing from Erewhon, we love your concept, but these specific three ingredients gotta go.

91
00:06:27,181 --> 00:06:32,472
Some brands even spend 6 to 12 months reformulating their products just to fit the Erewhon standard.

92
00:06:32,472 --> 00:06:36,303
And even after being accepted, the products remain on probation.

93
00:06:36,303 --> 00:06:37,982
If they don't sell well enough, they're out.

94
00:06:37,982 --> 00:06:44,522
But for these brands, it seems like it's all worth it because once you get that Erewhon stamp of approval, other retailers start calling.

95
00:06:44,522 --> 00:06:52,409
Industry insiders actually call this the Erewhon Effect, which is why so many emerging health brands try to launch exclusively at Erewhon first.

96
00:06:52,409 --> 00:06:55,541
From a business perspective, what Erewhon has created is brilliant.

97
00:06:55,541 --> 00:07:03,865
It's a two-sided marketplace where they curate brands for their consumers who trust their judgment while offering those brands access to their tastemaker audience.

98
00:07:03,865 --> 00:07:06,009
This isn't just a grocery store.

99
00:07:06,009 --> 00:07:10,041
It's basically a startup accelerator for kombucha and adaptogenic mushroom powders.

100
00:07:10,041 --> 00:07:15,709
Jokes aside, this is a big reason why a lot of people are down to dish out at Erewhon instead of going to Whole Foods.

101
00:07:15,709 --> 00:07:19,493
Erewhon, silly as it might sound, is on the cutting edge of these trends.

102
00:07:19,493 --> 00:07:22,240
They're first movers, and they're not just selling you food.

103
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:25,408
They're selling you first access to the next big thing in health.

104
00:07:25,408 --> 00:07:33,457
So if you're part of that target demographic that's wealthy, health-conscious, trend-aware, you could see how Erewhon is kind of the place to go.

105
00:07:33,457 --> 00:07:34,936
[门店经济] Now, let's talk numbers.

106
00:07:34,936 --> 00:07:38,419
You know I'm not gonna analyze this bad boy without going over some store economics.

107
00:07:38,419 --> 00:07:47,086
So as I mentioned, Erewhon's footprints are pretty small at about 10,000 to 15,000 square feet compared to traditional grocers at about 45,000 square feet.

108
00:07:47,086 --> 00:07:56,412
The amount of SKUs that it carries is not publicly available, but you can tell that it's a lot fewer than traditional grocers at 30,000 or more, and it's very tightly curated.

109
00:07:56,412 --> 00:08:01,223
So it's a lot like our friends at Trader Joe's with very picky product selection in smaller storefronts.

110
00:08:01,223 --> 00:08:02,520
Here's where it's different.

111
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:09,233
The average transaction size at Erewhon is between $85 and $100 compared to $40 at Whole Foods.&nbsp;

112
00:08:09,233 --> 00:08:13,845
Not only that, the profit margins are pretty nice and juicy compared to other grocers.

113
00:08:13,845 --> 00:08:24,035
For prepared food and beverages specifically, which account for almost half, 40% to 50% of Erewhon's sales, profit margins are about 35% compared to industry average of about 12%.

114
00:08:24,035 --> 00:08:27,244
So Erewhon is basically half restaurant, half grocer.

115
00:08:27,244 --> 00:08:34,933
And finally, given all that we know about Erewhon, it's no surprise that all 10 locations are in ultra-premium neighborhoods of Los Angeles.

116
00:08:34,933 --> 00:08:41,702
Beverly Hills, Studio City, Silver Lake, Pacific Palisades, Santa Monica, Venice, Calabasas, West Hollywood, Culver City, and Pasadena.

117
00:08:41,702 --> 00:08:46,598
And these ultra-premium locations, of course, are aiming for a very specific target audience.

118
00:08:46,598 --> 00:08:47,637
Let's discuss.

119
00:08:47,637 --> 00:08:49,669
[目标客群] The core Erewhon customer.&nbsp;

120
00:08:49,669 --> 00:09:03,771
Imagine that friend who casually brings up their wellness journey in every single convo, has eight-pack abs, drinks from Coconuts in Bali, has at least three different non-dairy milks in their fridge, 25 to 45 years old, household income well over $150,000.

121
00:09:03,771 --> 00:09:05,679
Very health-conscious and trend-aware.

122
00:09:05,679 --> 00:09:07,208
They're active on social media.

123
00:09:07,208 --> 00:09:10,699
Maybe an entertainment industry professional or a celebrity influencer.

124
00:09:10,699 --> 00:09:11,935
That's your guy.

125
00:09:11,935 --> 00:09:21,487
The way that Trader Joe's gets social media coverage for its kind of weird and quirky products, Erewhon gets it for its extremely high prices and very, very niche health-focused products.&nbsp;

126
00:09:21,487 --> 00:09:26,510
Plus, Erewhon has the added element of being only in LA, the entertainment capital of the world.

127
00:09:26,510 --> 00:09:32,685
So regular celebrity sightings include the Kardashians, Miley Cyrus, Kendrick Garfield, Jake Gyllenhaal.

128
00:09:32,685 --> 00:09:35,793
Last time I was here, I was in line directly next to David Dobrik.

129
00:09:35,793 --> 00:09:42,178
I don't see any in here today though, besides this up-and-coming YouTuber who likes to talk about grocery stores that she finds interesting.

130
00:09:42,178 --> 00:09:47,310
Anyway, to target these customers, naturally Erewhon only finds itself in these ultra-premium locations.

131
00:09:47,310 --> 00:09:51,611
But as always, there is more to it than it just being expensive food for celebrities.

132
00:09:51,611 --> 00:10:02,001
There is a value proposition alignment going on where Erewhon leverages health as luxury positioning, using wellness signaling and clean eating as a status symbol, which it kind of is.

133
00:10:02,001 --> 00:10:08,145
[食品公平] So this is a whole other rabbit hole that I went down in my research, the economics of food access in the U.S.

134
00:10:08,145 --> 00:10:21,223
According to the latest numbers from the U.S. Department of Agriculture, there are about 40 million Americans in the U.S. that live in designated food deserts, which are areas where it's either difficult or impossible to have access to affordable, healthy food.

135
00:10:21,223 --> 00:10:25,002
And different retailers have approached this market reality differently.

136
00:10:25,002 --> 00:10:33,675
Some, like Erewhon, focus exclusively in the premium segment, while others like Kroger's or Walmart have developed models that serve a broader demographic range.&nbsp;

137
00:10:33,675 --> 00:10:39,447
So there is a distinct market segmentation, and Erewhon certainly plays within the premium segment exceptionally well.

138
00:10:39,447 --> 00:10:47,131
But in some ways, it does feel wrong that healthy food is a status symbol when it is, in reality, out of reach for so many people.

139
00:10:47,131 --> 00:10:50,372
At the same time, I don't think it's Erewhon's responsibility to fix that.

140
00:10:50,372 --> 00:10:52,491
I think its very existence is perfectly fine.

141
00:10:52,491 --> 00:10:53,915
But yeah, it's a tricky one.

142
00:10:53,915 --> 00:10:55,641
Let me know your thoughts on this in the comments below.

143
00:10:55,641 --> 00:10:59,824
[定价逻辑] So we know the prices are high, but are they justified?

144
00:10:59,824 --> 00:11:01,272
Well, it's subjective.

145
00:11:01,272 --> 00:11:09,209
On one hand, Erewhon sources from small batch producers with local and beyond organic requirements, and it has limited distribution channels.

146
00:11:09,209 --> 00:11:11,340
So naturally, that's gonna cost.

147
00:11:11,340 --> 00:11:13,592
And a lot of that cost gets passed down to the consumer.

148
00:11:13,592 --> 00:11:17,647
On the other hand, at some point, it kind of feels like robbery, like this was $20.

149
00:11:17,647 --> 00:11:19,529
But there's clearly a market for it.

150
00:11:19,529 --> 00:11:22,907
And there's something to be said for the psychology behind premium pricing.

151
00:11:22,907 --> 00:11:24,969
It adds a layer of perceived value.

152
00:11:24,969 --> 00:11:36,642
So whether or not this fresh-pressed elderberry syrup from Erewhon is higher quality than an elderberry syrup that you might find at Whole Foods, you probably subconsciously assume that it is because it's more expensive.

153
00:11:36,642 --> 00:11:41,135
This health as a status symbol and exclusivity is reinforced through these higher prices.

154
00:11:41,135 --> 00:11:44,571
My personal take is through a bit more of an objective lens.

155
00:11:44,571 --> 00:11:57,558
So even if I can't justify myself to buy this $22 brown butter something something, because my perceived value of this brown butter something something does not outweigh how much I value $22.

156
00:11:57,558 --> 00:12:04,415
I do think the prices are justified in the sense that there's obviously a market equilibrium happening here where supply is meeting demand.

157
00:12:04,415 --> 00:12:06,731
So I don't fault Erewhon for setting these prices.

158
00:12:06,731 --> 00:12:07,731
I'm a businesswoman.

159
00:12:07,731 --> 00:12:11,515
At the same time, I do care about there being healthy, affordable food.

160
00:12:11,515 --> 00:12:16,646
So again, a little tricky and hard to say a definitive yes or no to the prices being justified.

161
00:12:16,646 --> 00:12:21,881
[扩张风险] Now, I find this section particularly interesting for Erewhon, the future of the store.

162
00:12:21,881 --> 00:12:27,971
Beginning with growth plans, Erewhon is planning on expanding to other markets, including New York City and Miami.

163
00:12:27,971 --> 00:12:35,241
In doing so, yes, it could target high income and health-conscious zip codes, but it would also run some huge risks.

164
00:12:35,241 --> 00:12:37,957
First of all, maintaining exclusivity while scaling.

165
00:12:37,957 --> 00:12:43,269
If you open up a whole bunch of new locations, it just kind of becomes less cool and exclusive.

166
00:12:43,269 --> 00:12:44,626
That's obvious psychology.

167
00:12:44,626 --> 00:12:47,736
What I'm more curious about is how would it fare in those cities?

168
00:12:47,736 --> 00:12:53,753
Sure, you have the expensive zip codes and health-conscious population, but what would Erewhon's distribution look like?

169
00:12:53,753 --> 00:12:55,360
Erewhon is known to source locally.&nbsp;

170
00:12:55,360 --> 00:13:00,690
And California alone produces a third of the vegetables and two thirds of the fruits and nuts in the US.

171
00:13:00,690 --> 00:13:07,448
Of course, you can ship things across the country, but Erewhon's supply chain starts looking a lot different if it opens up on the East Coast.

172
00:13:07,448 --> 00:13:14,469
And as someone born and raised in Los Angeles and living in New York for the last four years, I feel uniquely equipped to weigh in on this.

173
00:13:14,469 --> 00:13:18,535
[城市差异] I don't think Erewhon would work as well in New York.

174
00:13:18,535 --> 00:13:19,682
There, I said it.

175
00:13:19,682 --> 00:13:29,651
Yes, I could see a location opening up in Williamsburg or somewhere in Manhattan and it technically being successful, but the core audience for Erewhon just feels so distinctly LA.

176
00:13:29,651 --> 00:13:33,414
The healthy scene here is different than the healthy scene in New York.

177
00:13:33,414 --> 00:13:38,112
It's hard to explain, but in LA, wellness here feels more like a lifestyle statement.

178
00:13:38,112 --> 00:13:40,645
Looking good, feeling good, living your best life.

179
00:13:40,645 --> 00:13:44,511
In New York, it feels more about optimization and efficiency.

180
00:13:44,511 --> 00:13:47,355
Biohacking your way to surviving the city's intensity.

181
00:13:47,355 --> 00:13:49,367
Huge generalization, but that's how I feel.

182
00:13:49,367 --> 00:13:51,478
Now, would I still be happy if one opened up in New York?

183
00:13:51,478 --> 00:13:52,300
Of course.

184
00:13:52,300 --> 00:13:58,779
[经济风险] More broadly, a challenge that Erewhon and other luxury grocers face is vulnerability during an economic downturn.

185
00:13:58,779 --> 00:14:09,650
So turning to microeconomics for a second, food as a whole is generally considered an inelastic good, meaning that changes in price will not drastically affect consumer demand, which makes sense.

186
00:14:09,650 --> 00:14:10,548
We always need food.

187
00:14:10,548 --> 00:14:11,451
We're always going to need to buy it.

188
00:14:11,451 --> 00:14:13,759
This is not the case for luxury food.

189
00:14:13,759 --> 00:14:26,999
When people need to save some cash during an economic recession, even Erewhon shoppers might turn to Whole Foods or in LA specifically, Bristol Farms or Gelson's, which also have that healthy luxury positioning, but with slightly lower prices.

190
00:14:26,999 --> 00:14:31,975
Then there are other industry trends impacting Erewhon, like increasing scrutiny of health claims.

191
00:14:31,975 --> 00:14:35,171
Is sea moss gel actually delivering the health benefits that it promises?

192
00:14:35,171 --> 00:14:36,077
Let's see the research.

193
00:14:36,077 --> 00:14:46,847
There's also greater democratization of health products going on, where more affordable retailers like Amazon and Target are opening their own clean beauty and health and wellness brands at a fraction of the cost.

194
00:14:46,847 --> 00:14:52,630
So Erewhon will really need to stay ahead of the curve to maintain their first mover image in the space.

195
00:14:52,630 --> 00:14:58,398
